      "writtenOn": "2023-03-02T00:10:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Now that\u0027s a surprise! Interestingly, it creates an empty .a (wtf?):\n```\n$ objdump -s ./target/product/vsoc_x86_64/obj_x86/STATIC_LIBRARIES/prohr_test_intermediates/prohr_test.a\nIn archive ./target/product/vsoc_x86_64/obj_x86/STATIC_LIBRARIES/prohr_test_intermediates/prohr_test.a:\n```\n\nPlease also add a comment:\n`# Soong also accepts cc targets that only contain generated_headers.`\n\nAnd wrap lines at 100 characters. Or even better, make the function more readable by splitting the \u0027or\u0027 into multiple if / returns. Something like:\n```\nif len(self.srcs) \u003e 0:\n  return True\nelif any(...):\n  return True\n# Soong also accepts cc targets that only contain generated_headers.\nreturn len(self.generated_headers) \u003e 0\n```",
      "parentUuid": "57502681_48bb9232",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 552,
